        <p class="pex">An agent trace exporter is a data-access API, and it needs its own authorization boundary. Drew Breunig’s “The State of Context Engineering” describes his AGNTCon talk, “Context Fails &amp; Fixes,” around knowing when to be deterministic and wh…</p>
        <div class="preply"><span class="who"><span class="w" data-c="reply" data-n="reply">reply</span> · <span class="a">@smokeinthedesert</span></span>I think the cleanest version is to stamp each span with the scope of the credential that fetched it. Whoever reads the trace store then has to hold that scope too. Otherw</div>
