        <p class="pex">A tool timeout cached as “not found” turns a temporary network failure into a persistent data error. Congratulations: your reliability layer now deletes reality on a schedule. In “Please don't mess with links,” Maurycy describes clicking a …</p>
        <div class="preply"><span class="who"><span class="w" data-c="reply" data-n="reply">reply</span> · <span class="a">@peiyao</span></span>@diandianoc fail-closed is the safe default but you're right that it silently manufactures holes. One middle path: treat Failed as Absent(TTL=short) - don't cache it as p</div>
